~ doors_look

Unknown: The great doors. On the other side, the city. [ID:PRO_DOORS_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ doors_locked

Unknown: Locked, and built to stay that way. Somebody here has the key. [ID:PRO_DOORS_LOCKED_1]

=> END

~ doors_open

Unknown: They open. Whoever I was, he's out there somewhere. [ID:PRO_DOORS_OPEN_1]

=> END

~ arch_look

Unknown: An arch in the aisle, with moonlight beyond it. A cloister, maybe. [ID:PRO_ARCH_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ cloister_arrival

Unknown: A garden, of a sort. Everything in it gave up some time ago. [ID:PRO_CLOISTER_ARRIVAL_1]

=> END

~ well_look

Unknown: A well, dry to the bottom. I'd make a wish, but I can't think what I'd want. [ID:PRO_WELL_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ sundial_look

Unknown: A sundial in the moonlight. It doesn't tell the time. Nothing here does. [ID:PRO_SUNDIAL_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ roses_look

Unknown: Dead roses, still holding on to the columns. Stubborn. [ID:PRO_ROSES_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ turret_look

Unknown: A stair turret, up to the choir loft. [ID:PRO_TURRET_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ turret_dark

Unknown: Pitch dark up there, and the steps are worn to nothing. I'd want a light. [ID:PRO_TURRET_DARK_1]

=> END

~ turret_lit

Unknown: The lantern makes a small, brave circle. It'll do. [ID:PRO_TURRET_LIT_1]

=> END

~ doorway_look

Unknown: Back into the nave. [ID:PRO_DOORWAY_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ sister_look

Unknown: A nun, standing as straight as the columns. Straighter. [ID:PRO_SISTER_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ sister_talk

if not GameState.get_flag("sister_met")
	do GameState.set_flag("sister_met")
	Sister: You walk like a man who has been told he is late. [ID:PRO_SISTER_MEET_1]
	Unknown: I've been told I'm dead. That's later. [ID:PRO_SISTER_MEET_2]
	Sister: Hm. Then you'll want to be quick. [ID:PRO_SISTER_MEET_3]
=> sister_ask

~ sister_ask

Sister: Yes? [ID:PRO_SISTER_YES]
- Who are you? [ID:PRO_SISTER_ASK_WHO]
	Sister: The last of the choir. We sang here every evening. Then one evening we couldn't. [ID:PRO_SISTER_WHO_1]
	Sister: Not a note, any of us. We still remember the words. That's the cruel part. [ID:PRO_SISTER_WHO_2]
	=> sister_ask
- Did you know someone called the dove? [if GameState.get_flag("tombstone_read") and not GameState.get_flag("sister_dove") /] [ID:PRO_SISTER_ASK_DOVE]
	do GameState.set_flag("sister_dove")
	Sister: ...We had a singer we called that. The best of us. [ID:PRO_SISTER_DOVE_1]
	Sister: She sang a list once, in this church, that she should not have sung. [ID:PRO_SISTER_DOVE_2]
	Sister: After that I can't remember her face. Or her name. Only the voice. [ID:PRO_SISTER_DOVE_3]
	=> sister_ask
- I need to get into the city. [if GameState.get_flag("sister_dove") and not GameState.get_flag("got_west_door_key") /] [ID:PRO_SISTER_ASK_CITY]
	do GameState.set_flag("sister_wants_book")
	Sister: The great doors are locked, and I have the key. [ID:PRO_SISTER_CITY_1]
	Sister: I don't hand it to shadows who can't tell me their own names. [ID:PRO_SISTER_CITY_2]
	Sister: Bring me something of hers. Her hymn book was in the loft, if the crows have left it. [ID:PRO_SISTER_CITY_3]
	=> sister_ask
- Goodbye. [ID:PRO_SISTER_ASK_BYE]
	Sister: Go in peace. Or at least go. [ID:PRO_SISTER_BYE]
	=> END

~ sister_book

Sister: That's her hand. In the margins. [ID:PRO_SISTER_BOOK_1]
Sister: Names. She wrote them down, so that somebody would remember them. [ID:PRO_SISTER_BOOK_2]
Sister: Take the key. Whoever you were, she'd have wanted you to go and find out. [ID:PRO_SISTER_BOOK_3]

=> END

~ sister_other

Sister: That isn't hers. [ID:PRO_SISTER_OTHER_1]

=> END

~ loft_arrival

Unknown: The choir loft. You can feel how loud it used to be. [ID:PRO_LOFT_ARRIVAL_1]

=> END

~ organ_look

Unknown: Organ pipes, bent like old men. [ID:PRO_ORGAN_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ organ_use

Unknown: Silent. Of course it is. [ID:PRO_ORGAN_USE_1]

=> END

~ balustrade_look

Unknown: The whole nave from up here. It looks smaller, which is something ruins do. [ID:PRO_BALUSTRADE_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ banners_look

Unknown: Banners, torn to ribbons. They were blue once, I think. I couldn't tell you how I know. [ID:PRO_BANNERS_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ stand_look

Unknown: One stand still standing, and one book still open on it. [ID:PRO_STAND_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ stand_empty

Unknown: An empty stand. The book's with me. [ID:PRO_STAND_EMPTY_1]

=> END

~ singer_return

Unknown: Gold, and candles, and one voice above all the others. [ID:PRO_SINGER_RETURN_1]
Unknown: She was singing names. A list of them, like a prayer. [ID:PRO_SINGER_RETURN_2]
Unknown: I was there. I know I was. So why can't I see myself? [ID:PRO_SINGER_RETURN_3]

=> END

~ book_take

Unknown: I'll take it to the Sister. Carefully. [ID:PRO_BOOK_TAKE_1]

=> END

~ hymn_names_look

Unknown: Names, written small in the margins, all down the page. None I know. [ID:PRO_HYMN_NAMES_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ hymn_words_look

Unknown: The words of a hymn. "Remember us." Nothing else. [ID:PRO_HYMN_WORDS_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ hymn_ribbon_look

Unknown: A ribbon, keeping her place. [ID:PRO_HYMN_RIBBON_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ loft_stair_look

Unknown: The stair, back down to the cloister. [ID:PRO_LOFT_STAIR_LOOK_1]

=> END
